  "recipeCuisine": "France",
  "name": "Bearnaise Sauce",
  "text": "Bearnaise Sauce\n\nYield: 6\n\nPreparation time: 20 minutes\n\nIngredients\n\n2 tbsp white wine vinegar,\n\n3 tbsp snipped tarragon,\n\n30 g shallots (finely chopped),\n\n10 peppercorns (crushed),\n\n4 egg yolks,\n\n4 tbsp cold water,\n\n3 tbsp cold water,\n\n250 g freshly clarified butter (cooled to tepid),\n\n2 tbsp snipped chervil,\n\nJuice of ½ lemon,\n\nSalt and freshly ground pepper.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Combine the vinegar, 2 tbsp tarragon, the shallot and peppercorns in a small thick bottomed saucepan, and reduce by half over a low heat. Set aside to cool.\n\n2. When cool add the vinegar reduction to the egg yolks and cold water.\n\n3. Set the bowl over a pan of boiling water and whisk continuously.\n\n4. Gently increase the heat until creamy (8-10 minutes).\n\n5. Turn off the heat and add the clarified butter, initially a drop at a time, then in increasing quantities.\n\n6. Season with salt and pepper.",
  "recipeYield": "6",
  "prepTime": "PT20M",
